{
  "id": "u11-l01",
  "unit": "u11-plans",
  "title": "Tomorrow & next week",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**Time words that point forward.** কাল means both 'tomorrow' and 'yesterday'; the verb tells you which. **আগামীকাল** (*agamikal*) is always 'tomorrow', and **পরশু** (*porshu*) is 'the day after tomorrow'.\n\nFor 'next', put **আগামী** or the everyday **সামনের** before the time word: **আগামী সপ্তাহে** 'next week', **সামনের মাসে** 'next month', **আগামী বছর** 'next year'. **এই শুক্রবার** is 'this Friday'.\n\nYou already know some future verbs: **যাব** 'I'll go', **আসবে** 'will come', **কিনব** 'I'll buy'. The next lessons show the pattern behind them.\n\n**কাল দেখা হবে।** 'See you tomorrow.'",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "agamikal",
      "bn": "আগামীকাল",
      "tr": "agamikal",
      "en": "tomorrow",
      "notes": "Always 'tomorrow'. Plain কাল can mean 'tomorrow' or 'yesterday'; the verb decides."
    },
    {
      "id": "porshu",
      "bn": "পরশু",
      "tr": "porshu",
      "en": "the day after tomorrow",
      "notes": "With a past verb it means 'the day before yesterday', just as কাল is 'tomorrow' or 'yesterday'."
    },
    {
      "id": "agami",
      "bn": "আগামী",
      "tr": "agami",
      "en": "next",
      "notes": "আগামী সপ্তাহে 'next week', আগামী বছর 'next year'. A little more formal than সামনের. In Kolkata you also hear আসছে সপ্তাহে."
    },
    {
      "id": "shamner",
      "bn": "সামনের",
      "tr": "shamner",
      "en": "next (spoken)",
      "notes": "Literally 'of the front' (সামনে + -এর). Everyday word for 'next': সামনের মাসে 'next month'."
    },
    {
      "id": "mashe",
      "bn": "মাসে",
      "tr": "mashe",
      "en": "in the month",
      "notes": "মাস + -এ: আগামী মাসে 'next month'."
    },
    {
      "id": "dekha-hobe",
      "bn": "দেখা হবে",
      "tr": "dekha hobe",
      "en": "(we) will meet",
      "notes": "কাল দেখা হবে 'See you tomorrow'. You know it from আবার দেখা হবে."
    }
  ],
